  "description": "Jackson Pr. 14.23: N equal charges spaced evenly around one circle radiate only at the multiples of $N\\omega_0$ (N² times as strongly as one charge there), and a ring of many radiates almost nothing: a steady current does not radiate. The receiver now counts the band 0.6–2.6, which holds the first three harmonics ($\\omega_0$, $2\\omega_0$, $3\\omega_0$); keep it below 0.000013 per steradian. An opposite pair cancels $\\omega_0$, but its fields add at $2\\omega_0$. Space charges around the circle so that only a harmonic outside the band survives.",
